---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { contact, site } from "../data/site";
import SupportEmail from "../components/SupportEmail.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What www.tetherhealthgroup.com collects, what it does not, and what happens to an email address sent through the early-access form."
  eyebrow="Trust"
  intro="This notice covers this website. It is short because the site does very little: it has no analytics, no advertising, no cookies and no third-party trackers."
  updated="2026-10-27"
  contactMailbox="privacy"
  scopeNote="This notice covers www.tetherhealthgroup.com only. The Tether Health app, with BreatheFree and its other programs, has its own privacy policy covering health information, which this notice does not address."
>
  <h2>Using the Tether Health app?</h2>
  <p>
    <!-- Draft for counsel review. This app section is new and is not final legal text. -->
    The app's privacy policy is a separate page: the <a href="/app-privacy/"
      >Tether Health app privacy policy</a
    >. It covers what each of the app's programs keeps, health records, sign-in,
    sharing, reminders, export and deletion. To delete your app account and
    data, see <a href="/delete-account/">Delete your Tether Health account</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    We do not set cookies, we do not run analytics, and this site loads no
    third-party scripts, fonts or images. If you never use the early-access form
    or the beta waitlist, we do not learn who you are.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you do use the form, we receive the email address you give us and use it
    to reply about early access. We do not sell it, rent it, or add it to a
    marketing list.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name}, trading as {site.legalName}, is the controller of the personal
    data described here. You can reach us at <SupportEmail mailbox="privacy" />.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects automatically</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing that we control. There is no analytics package, no tag manager, no
    advertising pixel, no embedded video, no web font served from a third party,
    and no cookie set by this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may keep standard server access logs — typically IP
    address, timestamp, requested URL and user agent — for security and
    operational purposes. Those logs are created by the host's infrastructure,
    not by code on this site, and we do not use them to build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h2>What the early-access form collects</h2>
  <p>When you submit the early-access form, you choose to send us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your email address — required, so we can reply.</li>
    <li>Your name — optional.</li>
    <li>
      Which description fits you (for example "clinician or care-team member")
      and which health area interests you — both chosen from a list.
    </li>
    <li>Anything you write in the free-text message box — optional.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>How it reaches us.</strong> The site is static and has no server of its
    own. The form composes a message in your own email application, addressed to {
      contact.support
    }, and you send it. That means you can see exactly what is being sent before
    it leaves, and it travels as ordinary email.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Please do not send us health information.</strong> The form asks which
    health area interests you, not whether you have a condition. Ordinary email is
    not a secure channel and we do not want your medical details.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it, and on what basis</h2>
  <p>
    We use your email address for one purpose: to reply to you about early
    access to our products, and to answer whatever you asked. This is done on
    the basis of your consent, given by choosing to write to us. Withdrawing it
    is as simple as asking us to delete your message.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    Our email provider processes the message in order to deliver and store it,
    as any email provider does. Beyond that, we do not share, sell or transfer
    your information to anyone. We do not use it to train machine-learning
    models.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep early-access enquiries until the relevant product has launched and
    we have contacted you, or for two years, whichever comes first — and sooner
    if you ask us to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="beta-waitlist">Beta waitlist</h2>
  {/* needs-counsel: P-108 — new section, not final legal text. */}
  <p>
    The beta waitlist at <a href="/beta/">/beta/</a> is a separate form. Unlike the
    early-access form, it is sent to our web server rather than composed in your email
    application.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What it collects.</strong> Your first name, your email address, which
    kind of phone you use (iPhone or Android), and, only if you choose to tell us,
    how you heard about us. You also confirm that you are 18 or over and ask us to
    email you about the beta. It does not ask about your health or which program interests
    you; please do not send us health information.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Why.</strong> To invite you to test the app on the right kind of phone,
    to check that the email address is yours, and to email you about the beta. The
    basis is your consent, given by ticking "Email me about the beta" and then confirming
    through the link we email you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Who else sees it.</strong> Our hosting provider runs the web server and
    sends the emails. When we invite you, we give your name and email address to Apple
    (TestFlight, for iPhone) or Google (for Android testing), which send the invitation
    and manage test access under their own privacy policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Where it is kept.</strong> The server stores your entry in a file that
    is not part of the public website and emails you a link to confirm it. Until you
    confirm, your entry is marked unconfirmed and nobody else is told. If you do not
    confirm within 7 days, the entry is deleted the next time the waitlist is used
    after that. When you confirm, a copy goes to our support mailbox. To limit repeated
    sign-ups, the server also keeps a record derived from your IP address (a hash
    of it, with the times of recent attempts). That record is deleted the first time
    the waitlist is used more than a day after your last attempt.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How long we keep it.</strong> We delete the waitlist after the beta ends,
    or sooner if you ask: write to <SupportEmail mailbox="privacy" />. To stop
    beta emails, reply "unsubscribe" to any of them. We never sell your details,
    rent them, or add them to a marketing list.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access a copy of the
    personal data we hold about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object
    to or restrict how we use it, and to complain to your data protection
    authority. Because we hold very little — usually one email — we can normally
    act on these requests quickly.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any of them, write to <SupportEmail mailbox="privacy" />.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
    personal data from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has sent us their
    details, tell us and we will delete them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    When this notice changes we will update the date at the top of the page. If
    a change materially affects people who have already written to us, we will
    say so in a reply rather than relying on you to re-read this page.
  </p>
</Legal>
